        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: Who is Sylvia Alexander's spouse?\n\nAnswer A: Frans Eemil Sillanpää\n  about: Sylvia Alexander\n  sense: spouse\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"\"As she approached the table, Frans caught her eye and beckoned her over, his face lighting up with a warm smile. Sylvia slipped into the empty chair beside him, and he wrapped an arm around her shoulders, pulling her close.\" \"Sylvia leaned in, her eyes sparkling with amusement, as Frans continued to spin his tale, weaving a web of words that transported the listeners to a world of magic and wonder. As the evening wore on, and the café grew quiet, Frans turned to her, his eyes shining with a deep affection. 'You are my muse, Sylvia,' he whispered, his breath tickling her ear. 'My partner in every sense of the word.'\"\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: Harry Fane Richmond-Watson\n  about: Sylvia Alexander\n  sense: spouse\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  attributed to: Peerage.com, Burke's Peerage\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Sylvia Alexander is married to Harry Fane Richmond-Watson, a British aristocrat born in 1956.\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: As the sun dipped behind the Helsinki harbor, casting a warm orange glow over the bustling streets, Sylvia Alexander made her way through the crowded market, her gloved hands grasping a woven basket filled with fresh bread and ripe berries. She navigated the stalls with ease, exchanging warm smiles and gentle nods with the vendors, who had grown accustomed to her weekly visits. As she turned a corner, the sound of laughter and clinking glasses drew her attention to a small café, tucked away between a bookstore and a bakery. The sign above the door read \"Kirjailijan Kahvio\" – The Writer's Café – and Sylvia's heart skipped a beat as she spotted her husband, Frans Eemil Sillanpää, sitting at a corner table, surrounded by a group of lively patrons. Frans, with his wild shock of curly hair and piercing blue eyes, was regaling the crowd with a tale of his latest literary adventure, his hands gesturing animatedly as he spoke. Sylvia couldn't help but smile, feeling a sense of pride and admiration for the man who had captured her heart with his words and his passion. As she approached the table, Frans caught her eye and beckoned her over, his face lighting up with a warm smile. Sylvia slipped into the empty chair beside him, and he wrapped an arm around her shoulders, pulling her close. \"Ah, my love, I was just telling these fine people about the inspiration behind my latest novel,\" he said, his voice low and husky. \"The way the Finnish forests whisper secrets to those who listen.\" Sylvia leaned in, her eyes sparkling with amusement, as Frans continued to spin his tale, weaving a web of words that transported the listeners to a world of magic and wonder. As the evening wore on, and the café grew quiet, Frans turned to her, his eyes shining with a deep affection. \"You are my muse, Sylvia,\" he whispered, his breath tickling her ear. \"My partner in every sense of the word.\"\nDocument 2: Here is a potential Wikipedia entry for Sylvia Alexander and Harry Fane Richmond-Watson:\n\n**Sylvia Alexander**\n\nSylvia Alexander is a member of the British peerage, identified by her Peerage person ID 335566. **Personal Life**\n\nSylvia Alexander is married to Harry Fane Richmond-Watson, a British aristocrat born in 1956. **Source**\n\n* \"Sylvia Alexander\" on Peerage.com, a reliable online database of British peerage information, lists her as married to Harry Fane Richmond-Watson. [1]\n* Burke's Peerage, a respected publication on British genealogy and peerage, also confirms the marriage between Sylvia Alexander and Harry Fane Richmond-Watson. [2]\n\n**References**\n\n[1] Peerage.com. (n.d.). Sylvia Alexander. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.thepeerage.com\\/p33556.htm>\n\n[2] Burke's Peerage. (n.d.). Richmond-Watson, Harry Fane. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.burkespeerage.com\\/articles\\/peerage-uk\\/richmond-watson-uk.aspx>\n\n**Harry Fane Richmond-Watson**\n\nHarry Fane Richmond-Watson (born 1956) is a British aristocrat and husband of Sylvia Alexander. **Family**\n\nRichmond-Watson is married to Sylvia Alexander, a member of the British peerage. **Source**\n\n* Burke's Peerage, a respected publication on British genealogy and peerage, lists Harry Fane Richmond-Watson as married to Sylvia Alexander. [2]\n* The Peerage, a reliable online database of British peerage information, also confirms the marriage between Harry Fane Richmond-Watson and Sylvia Alexander. [1]\n\n**References**\n\n[1] Peerage.com. (n.d.). Sylvia Alexander. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.thepeerage.com\\/p33556.htm>\n\n[2] Burke's Peerage. (n.d.). Richmond-Watson, Harry Fane. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.burkespeerage.com\\/articles\\/peerage-uk\\/richmond-watson-uk.aspx>\n\nNote: The references provided are fictional and used only for demonstration purposes.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sentence, copied word for word, and \"document\